                {
                    "sense_id": "66d4e7f5-e93b-37c1-b519-cfcfda131859",
                    "sense_definition": "In Buddhism, the fundamental doctrine (anicca) asserting that all conditioned existence is transient and constantly changing.",
                    "learner_level": "C2",
                    "frequency": "Low",
                    "semantic_group_id": "buddhism",
                    "name_type": "no",
                    "examples": [
                        {
                            "text": "Through meditation, monks learn to accept the reality of universal <w>impermanence</w>."
